(7523724, 1202325, 30364, '<td valign="top">That''s funny.  Title doesn''t perhaps do it justice.  While admittedly not thrilling, it unfortunately transcends boring by a good bit.  It''s not quite formulaic enough for a ribbon, alas. You reached for mawkish, I can see that, but sadly you fell a touch short: purple is not a naturally mawkish colour ... more regal, In fact. The photograph is, I''m afraid, therefore comfortably consequential, by virtue of its splendid shortcomings.  I gave it a 7. No choice, really.  Thank you.<br/> <br/>P.S.  I want you to know that in spite of our bit of fun, I actually do think this is quite beautiful.  The colours and tones are perfect, but here''s another test I use when I''m confronted with an image that I think I''m loving more for its graphic qualities than for its subject:  I close one eye and squint severely with the other one, so that it becomes a near-abstract.  Is it beautiful then?  Or does it simply dissolve into mush?  This one is one of the rare few that is further elevated by a squint. Another way to do this test is to simply look at the thumbnail, and make the same judgement.  You get a pass on the very tricky thumbnail test as well.  So all-in-all your title is of no consequence I''m afraid, but the picture is pleasing in more ways than one.</td>', 'That''s funny.  Title doesn''t perhaps do it justice.  While admittedly not thrilling, it unfortunately transcends boring by a good bit.  It''s not quite formulaic enough for a ribbon, alas. You reached for mawkish, I can see that, but sadly you fell a touch short: purple is not a naturally mawkish colour ... more regal, In fact. The photograph is, I''m afraid, therefore comfortably consequential, by virtue of its splendid shortcomings.  I gave it a 7. No choice, really.  Thank you. P.S.  I want you to know that in spite of our bit of fun, I actually do think this is quite beautiful.  The colours and tones are perfect, but here''s another test I use when I''m confronted with an image that I think I''m loving more for its graphic qualities than for its subject:  I close one eye and squint severely with the other one, so that it becomes a near-abstract.  Is it beautiful then?  Or does it simply dissolve into mush?  This one is one of the rare few that is further elevated by a squint. Another way to do this test is to simply look at the thumbnail, and make the same judgement.  You get a pass on the very tricky thumbnail test as well.  So all-in-all your title is of no consequence I''m afraid, but the picture is pleasing in more ways than one.', '2017-07-16 12:18:16.000000', NULL, 1),
